hat exact additive closure\n+  and invokes the unbounded predicate for every epoch. The genuine D.110c-a/b\n+  path consequently supplies a causal epoch-2 closure-growth control rather\n+  than a synthetic census.\n+- `packages/node/src/creator-adoption.ts` cold reopen and pending recovery both\n+  call `openCurrentAnchorTrust()` on the predecessor record, require the\n+  caller's genesis anchor/signature bytes to equal that predecessor record,\n90→+  assign `currentEpoch: 0`/`successorEpoch: 1`, require\n+  `v3-live-generation-1` followed by `v3-live-generation-2`, and use literal\n+  epoch-0/epoch-1 ACL checks. Those branches therefore fail on a genuine active\n+  epoch-2 room even though D.110c-b has already authenticated and activated it.\n+- `packages/node/src/internal/creator-room-head.ts` and the accepted 0b0 room\n+  authority already own exact copied `(objectId, epoch, currentAnchorDigest)`\n+  validation. The checkpoint opener consumes that authenticated value; it does\n+  not read a maximum epoch, trust the generation being opened, or create a new\n+  floor.\n+- `packages/node/src/internal/closed-epoch-cleanup.ts` already requires two\n100→+  complete `Superseded` rollback generations. 0b1 may prove and preserve the\n+  older/floor generation as the immediate-predecessor carrier, but it may not\n+  delete a generation or weaken D.109 availability/snapshot/outbox authority.\n+\n+The end-state has one owner per concept. The new protocol subpath alone opens a\n+bounded creator checkpoint; the existing successor opener remains the one-step\n+hot/QC primitive it reuses. The new control-plane subpath alone classifies a\n+bounded closure advance; the existing predicate remains the exact 0→1\n+compatibility path. Node continues to own storage lineage and product\n+composition, and its existing room-head owner remains the sole local floor\n110→+shape/oracle. An unexported singleton-registry mint callback may be added inside\n+protocol-v3 only so the reviewed opene